ina-Georgia, Tennessee-LSU and more.","published":"2026-11-16T23:15:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50498153/2026-college-football-week-12-top-25-betting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Illinois may turn to third-string QB Boyd after Houser injury","description":"Illinois might turn to third-string quarterback Carson Boyd this week against No. 15 Iowa after starter Katin Houser suffered a broken nose Friday at UCLA that required surgery.","published":"2026-11-16T21:42:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504718/illinois-turn-third-string-qb-boyd-houser-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Rivers says NC State only college job he would have taken","description":"New coach Philip Rivers said NC State was the only college job he would have taken.","published":"2026-11-16T22:20:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504530/rivers-says-nc-state-only-college-job-taken","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest up to No. 10 in AP poll as top teams avoid upsets","description":"Wake Forest's move up to No. 10 was the only week-over-week change atop the AP poll as the top nine teams remained unchanged.","published":"2026-11-16T20:48:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504044/wake-forest-no-10-ap-poll-top-teams-avoid-upsets","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas' Manning to participate in senior day, mum on future","description":"Texas quarterback Arch Manning said Monday he will participate in Saturday's senior day ceremonies despite having one year of eligibility remaining.","published":"2026-11-16T20:31:37.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503997/texas-arch-manning-participate-senior-day","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wisconsin safety Matt Jung to have season-ending ankle surgery","description":"Wisconsin safety Matt Jung will undergo season-ending ankle surgery, the school announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-16T21:10:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503973/wisconsin-safety-matt-jung-season-ending-ankle-surgery","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas DL Hero Kanu undergoes season-ending surgery on arm","description":"Texas starting defensive tackle Hero Kanu had season-ending surgery on his arm Monday, coach Steve Sarkisian announced.","published":"2026-11-16T20:55:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503942/texas-dl-hero-kanu-undergoes-season-ending-surgery-arm","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Cignetti: Narrative surrounding Indiana serves as motivation","description":"Indiana coach Curt Cignetti thinks his team's accomplishments continue to be unfairly discredited, and he's using it for motivation as the Hoosiers chase another national title.","published":"2026-11-16T19:38:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503441/narrative-surrounding-indiana-serves-motivation","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"AP college football Week 11 poll reaction: What's next for Top 25","description":"A look at the AP rankings, along with a key stat and what's ahead for each team.","published":"2026-11-16T20:51:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50484987/week-11-ap-college-football-poll-reaction-next-top-25","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5077638/bray-hubbard","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bray_Hubbard"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Bray Hubbard","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bray_Hubbard","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:32Z","intro":"Brayson \"Bray\" Hubbard (born February 14, 2005) is an American college football safety for the Alabama Crimson Tide.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Hubbard was born in Ocean Springs, Mississippi and attended Ocean Springs High School. He was rated as a three-star recruit and committed to play college football for the Alabama Crimson Tide over offers from FAU, Mississippi State, Navy, Tulane, and Southern Miss."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a freshman in 2023, Hubbard appeared in nine games for Alabama, notching one tackle. In week 8 of the 2024 season, he notched nine tackles in a 24–17 loss to Tennessee, after replacing injured starter Keon Sabb. Heading into week 9, Hubbard was named the team's starting safety due to Sabb's injury. In his first career start, he totaled seven tackles and an interception in a win over Missouri. Hubbard went viral for jogging during a play that resulted in a touchdown versus Florida State in 2025."}]}}